  <h1>Affiliate Program Agreement</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated: June 29, 2026</p>

  <p>This Affiliate Program Agreement ("Agreement") governs participation in the Website Support Studio affiliate program operated by Corriston Consulting ("we," "us," or "our"). By enrolling or promoting our services as an affiliate ("you" or "Affiliate"), you agree to this Agreement.</p>

  <h2>1. Enrollment</h2>
  <p>To participate, you must be approved by us and receive a unique referral code and/or link. We may approve or decline applicants at our discretion. You must provide accurate information and keep it current for commission payments.</p>

  <h2>2. Commissions</h2>
  <p>You earn a commission on qualifying sales that are attributed to your unique code or link, at the rate communicated to you in writing at enrollment. A sale qualifies when it is completed, paid in full, and not refunded, charged back, or canceled. Commissions are not earned on your own purchases (self-referrals) or on fraudulent or invalid orders.</p>

  <h2>3. Attribution</h2>
  <p>Sales are attributed using your unique discount code at checkout and/or referral-link tracking (which may use cookies). Where both a code and a link could apply, we determine attribution in good faith. We rely on our payment and tracking systems as the record of qualifying sales.</p>

  <h2>4. Payment Terms</h2>
  <p>Commissions are calculated on completed, non-refunded sales and paid on a periodic basis (for example, monthly), subject to any minimum payout threshold and after any applicable refund/clawback period. You are responsible for any taxes on amounts you earn. You are an independent contractor, not an employee, partner, or agent of Corriston Consulting.</p>

  <h2>5. Required Disclosures (FTC)</h2>
  <div class="note">
    <p>You <strong>must clearly and conspicuously disclose</strong> your financial relationship with us whenever you promote our services — for example with "#ad," "#affiliate," "paid partnership," or a plain statement that you earn a commission. Disclosures must be hard to miss and placed where your audience will see them before engaging. This is required by the U.S. Federal Trade Commission and applies to every post, story, video, email, and page where you promote us.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>6. Prohibited Practices</h2>
  <p>You may not: make false, misleading, or unsubstantiated claims about our services or pricing; promise specific results we do not guarantee; spam or send unsolicited messages; bid on our trademarks or run misleading paid ads; impersonate us; post our codes on coupon/deal aggregator sites without permission; or engage in any unlawful or deceptive activity. Violations may result in forfeited commissions and termination.</p>

  <h2>7. Use of Brand Materials</h2>
  <p>We may provide approved logos, images, and copy. You may use them only to promote our services and only as provided, and you may not modify our marks or imply endorsement, partnership, or employment beyond the affiliate relationship.</p>

  <h2>8. Term &amp; Termination</h2>
  <p>Either party may end this Agreement at any time. We may suspend or terminate your participation and withhold commissions for violations of this Agreement or suspected fraud. Commissions earned on valid, completed sales before termination remain payable, subject to refund/clawback adjustments.</p>

  <h2>9. Disclaimers &amp; Limitation of Liability</h2>
  <p>The program is provided "as is." To the fullest extent permitted by law, our total liability to you under this Agreement will not exceed the commissions payable to you in the three months before the event giving rise to the claim.</p>

  <h2>10. Governing Law</h2>
  <p>This Agreement is governed by the laws of the United States and the state in which Corriston Consulting maintains its principal place of business, without regard to conflict-of-laws rules.</p>

  <h2>11. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about the affiliate program? Contact Corriston Consulting at <a href="mailto:gary.corriston@gmail.com">gary.corriston@gmail.com</a>.</p>

